synchronized block: It can be written inside any executable block/context, such as:

✅ Method
✅ Constructor
✅ Instance initializer block
✅ Static initializer block

But not directly inside the class body.

class Test {

    static {
        synchronized (Test.class) {   // ✅
            // code
        }
    }

    Test() {
        synchronized (Test.class) {   // ✅
            // code
        }
    }

    void display() {
        synchronized (Test.class) {   // ✅
            // code
        }
    }
}
